# Sprint 16a: exclude internal/historical docs from the fresh public archive.
# git archive PRUNES export-ignored directories wholesale, so we exclude leaf
# paths (subdirs with nothing to keep, plus individual files) rather than the
# whole docs/ tree — that keeps docs/release-notes/v1.0.0.md (the launch note,
# read by release.yml) in the public archive.
docs/adr/** export-ignore
docs/sprints/** export-ignore
docs/architecture.md export-ignore
docs/bugs.md export-ignore
docs/javalens_feeback_from_cursor.md export-ignore
docs/refactoring-tool-contract.md export-ignore
docs/upgrade-checklist.md export-ignore
docs/upstream-parity-v1.4.2.md export-ignore
npm/** export-ignore
CHANGELOG.md export-ignore

# Sprint 28a (1a step 1): pin line endings at checkout. The first-ever Windows
# matrix run failed 19 refactoring-parity tests on ONE cause: no EOL policy, so
# Git for Windows (core.autocrlf=true by default) checked out fixtures AND
# goldens as CRLF, and a byte-exact comparison against LF-rendered engine
# output could never match. The engine's output was character-identical across
# OSes — the inputs were not. This pins the INPUTS; the comparison stays
# byte-exact. Windows script formats keep their required CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.png binary
*.jar binary
*.zip binary
*.class binary
